<!-- Trijicon VCOG 1-6x24 300 BLK segmented-circle BDC, from Trijicon's reticle sheet.
     Framed as the sheet draws it: the 6x field of view, 25 mils (84.5 MOA) in radius.
     The horizontal stadia are marked every 5 mils = 16.9 MOA; the sheet's "16.9 MOA x 12"
     says the etched pattern carries 12 of them, so it continues one mark past this field.
     Centre crosshair = 19 in at 100 m and the 100 m zero (supersonic); its bottom end is
     the 200 m supersonic hold. Stadia below are 300, 400, 500 and 600 m, each 19 in wide
     at its own range. The three diamonds are subsonic holds - 25/50 m, 100 m, 150 m -
     centred on the hold. Ring: 25 MOA gaps on both axes, 66.4 MOA over the outer corners
     = 19 in at 25 m.
     Ladder computed for 115gr BC 0.290 G1 at 2330 fps (supersonic) and 208gr A-MAX
     BC 0.648 G1 at 1010 fps (subsonic), 2.9 in sight height (the V-COG's tall integral
     mount), 1:8 RH, ICAO sea level, zeroed with the supersonic load at 100 m. Both loads
     were identified from the sheet's own geometry (0.17 and 0.18 MOA RMS over every mark
     it draws). The 25/50 m diamond sits on the 50 m hold; 25 m is 0.54 MOA lower. -->
